<BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/><BRL/></TAB></ENG><BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>FML Components</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Components, such as sleeves, boots, must be factory prefabricated from the FML material and have the same fabrication characteristics.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>Fuels for Testing FML</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Other materials, in addition to the FML, must be resistant to the fuel or fuels being stored.  Fuels, as required or mentioned by this specification, 
must be in accordance with the following:</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL>Motor Gasoline (Mogas)</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Mogas must be in accordance with <RID>ASTM D4814</RID> REV B.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>Diesel</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Diesel must be in accordance with <RID>CID A-A-52557</RID>.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>No. 2 and No. 4 Fuel Oils</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Oils must be in accordance with <RID>ASTM D396</RID>.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>JP-4 and JP-5</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Fuels must be in accordance with <RID>MIL-DTL-5624</RID>.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>JP-7</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Fuel must be in accordance with <RID>MIL-DTL-38219</RID>.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>JP-8</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Fuel must be in accordance with <RID>MIL-DTL-83133</RID>.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>ASTM Fuel B</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>ASTM Fuel B as referenced in this section must be in accordance with <RID>ASTM D471</RID>.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
</SPT></SPT><SPT><TTL><SUB>GEOTEXTILE FABRIC</SUB></TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Provide geotextile fabric between sand and underside of flexible membrane liner under the tank bottom with the following properties:</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TAB>
<WBK>
